**Summary of the reconstruction:**

The binary is a single-function program. `main` (`FUN_004004b6`) is the only program logic; `FUN_00400400/0410/0440` are empty `_init`/`__libc_csu_init`/`__libc_csu_fini` stubs (excluded per strategy).

The program takes an integer argument, allocates `malloc((byte)(n<<2))` bytes, then writes `n` × 4 bytes into it — so for any `n` where `n*4 > 255` (i.e. `n ≥ 65`), the allocation is too small and the fill loop overflows the heap buffer. This is the vulnerability the reconstruction preserves exactly (no "fixes" applied).

